// Pure percussion, no pitches. K (kick): the heel of the picking hand drops on string 6 and the
// top beside it, a damped thud (x on string 6). S (snare): flat i-m-a slap strings 1-4 onto the
// frets (dead notes with the slap mark). Bar 2 doubles the kick on 3 and the "and" of 3.
\title "Kick and snare on the guitar"
\tempo 90
\track ("Guitar" "Gtr.") { instrument acousticguitarsteel }
\staff { tabs }
\ts (4 4)
:4 x.6{txt "K"} (x.4 x.3 x.2 x.1){s} x.6{txt "K"} (x.4 x.3 x.2 x.1){s} |
:4 x.6{txt "K"} (x.4 x.3 x.2 x.1){s} :8 x.6{txt "K"} x.6{txt "K"} :4 (x.4 x.3 x.2 x.1){s}
